  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe combine elements of the simulated annealing approach from Strategy 1 with a spectral clustering method inspired by the separability objective proposed in Strategy 2. The core idea is to enforce hard separability conditions that minimize a \"bad overlap\" term, which penalizes cases where h(x) and 1-h(x+k) become too similar. This is achieved by:\n1. Introducing a soft penalty term (-bad_overlap_regularizer * penalty(h)) that encourages hard separability\n2. Using the parent solution as a springboard for search\n3. Alternating between gradient-based refinement and separability-enforcing steps\n\nThe algorithm \"projects\" away from configurations where h overlaps too much with its shifted versions, which addresses a key bottleneck in the original optimization-local optima often arise when h matches 1-h at shifted positions.\n\nMathematical specification:\nVariables: h[0:2] 360-point model in [0,1] with \u222bh dx=1\nObjective: E(h) = [max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx * dx] + \u03bb S(h)\nWhere S(h) = \u2211_{i,j} sigmoid(d(h_i,1-h_j))  penalizing similarity\n\nConstraints: 0\u2264h_i\u22641; \u2211h_i = 360/2 exactly\n\nImplementation:\n1. Parent validation and initialization:\n   - Adjust parent sum to exactly 180 (360/2)\n   - Clip to [0,1]\n   - Augment with auxiliary initializations (binary patterns, uniform distribution)\n\n2. Optimization algorithm:\n   - Maximum total time: 1100 seconds\n   - Breakdown: 35% annealing, 45% gradient refinement, 20% fallback\n   - Pseudocode structure:\n     function optimize_step(h, lambda_value, mode)\n        if mode == 'anneal':\n            for 25% max_eval:\n                h_bin = convert(h, 'binary')\n                h_bin, bad_overlap = binary_sa_mod(h_bin)\n                if improve or random:\n                    h = interpolate(h_bin)\n        elif mode == 'gradient':\n            w = compute_weights(bad_overlap)\n            z = project_away_weights(w)\n            h, bad_overlap = projected_gradient(z)\n\n3. Separability handling:\n   - bad_overlap_regularizer =  ((current_score - prev_score) / 0.01) if improve\n   - penalty(h) = maximum correlation among similar patterns\n   - BinarySA_mod(): enhanced simulator annealer focusing on separability\n   - Projected_gradient: L1-projection into separable space\n\n4. Candidate selection:\n   - Maintain watch-list of top 3 diversions\n   - Dynamic resolution doubling when time permits (n=360 to n=720)\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- Initializations: \n  1. Binary particle swarms (20% density)\n  2. Log-periodic decomposition\n  3. Uniform hill-climb from initial parent\n- Hyper-parameters:\n  lambda_min=0.001, lambda_max=0.05\n  swap_rate={0.6, 0.75, 0.8} during anneal\n  kernel=[gaussian, logistic] for penalty terms\n\nComputebudget:\n- Core search: 700s\n- Repair/validate: 200s\n- Upsample: 150s\n- Safeguards: 50s\n\nValidation requirements:\n1. After every candidate generation:\n   - Verify 0\u2264h_i\u22641\n   - Enforce exact sum=180\n   - Re-evaluate C5 with original code\n\nReturn format:\n(h[0:720], C5_bound, n_points) -> (vector, float, int)\n\nDetails of separability handling function (to be implemented):\n\ndef compute_bad_overlap_matrix(h):\n    # Cross-compute similarity between every i-j pair\n    weight = 0.95  # sigmoid weight\n    n = h.shape[0]\n    penalties = np.zeros([n,n])\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            # Approximate similarity with linear interpolation\n            penalties[i,j] = np.tanh(abs(i-j)*0.1) * h[i] * (1-h[j]) + np.random.normal(0,0.1)\n    return np.average(penalties)\n\ndef binary_sa_mod(h_bin):\n    # Enhanced simmetr \n    n = h_bin.shape[0]\n    target = n/2  # 180\n    penalties = compute_bad_overlap_matrix(h_bin)\n    T0 = 0.5 * time_left  # initial temperature\n    decay = 1-1e-6\n    best_overall = h_bin.copy()\n    best_overall = adjust_sum(best_overall, target)\n    best_overlap_val = compute_c5(best_overall)\n    n_iters = 0\n    for T in np.logspace(0, -8, num=500, endpoint=True):\n        while time_left > T:  # >=\n            if n_iters >= 1e6: break\n            # Random swap attempt\n            if np.random.random() < swap_rates[current_iteration]:\n                i,j = random_indices\n                # Compute overlap consequences without mutation\n                original_overlap = penalties[i] + penalties[j] + np.random.uniform(-0.1,0.1)\n                # Update structure\n                h_bin[i] = 0 if h_bin[j]==1 else 1\n                h_bin[j] = 0 if h_bin[i]==1 else 1\n                # Recompute overlap\n                new_overlap = penalties[i] + penalties[j] + np.random.uniform(-0.1,0.1)\n                delta = new_overlap - original_overlap\n                if (np.random.random() < np.exp(-delta/T)) or (delta<0):\n                    best_if_improve(best_overall)\n            n_iters +=1\n        T *= decay\n    return h_bin, best_overlap_val\n\nThe complete implementation must include helper functions for exact_sum, compute_binary_penalty, and projected_gradient. The key innovation is combining the separation penalty with a gradient projection into a dynamical optimization space.\n\nWe maintain three priorities:\n1. Preserve separability\n2. Improve score\n3. Maintain Varations\n\nThe fallback mechanism transforms parent to binary equivalent and then applies separability constraints.",
